T:Aguinaldo: Puerto Rican Christmas song in two voices
C:traditional (Puerto Rico)
O:Puerto Rico
R:aguinaldo
S:Allena Luce, Canciones populares (New York: Silver, Burdett, 1921), "Aguinaldo (Si me dan pasteles)", p. 3
N:THE PLATE: G minor, 2/4; an instrumental ritornello (two systems, Fine at the first ending), then the sung verse with a repeat, its melody doubled in thirds in the pianist's right hand, the words above; Luce's preface: collected from students of the University of Puerto Rico, versions chosen by their vote.
N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): p. 3 from the archive.org scan (about 290 dpi); staff lines found beside each chord and both heads of every chord measured against them; durations read from the scan; every bar checked to make two quarters.
N:THE RITORNELLO (transcribed 2026-11-11): the top line of Luce's right hand, with her two endings; the second ends on the chord F sharp, c, d (D7), leading into the verse. Read against staff lines found at each note (the page is skewed), checked bar by bar.
N:UNCERTAIN: the first note of the ritornello's bar 8 (d, close to c); bar 7's lower voice (see the next step); the last bar's "gen-te" on one chord; the tempo is ours.
